--- which of several siblings is reached, and what counts as 'same' ---

two same-basis siblings, both sorting before bettercad-deps:
  exit=1  Qt DLLs deployed=0
  Unable to find dependent libraries of C:\Users\uqhas\AppData\Local\bettercad-aaa\gnu-16-mingw-amd64\bin\Qt6Core.dll
  -> the FIRST in name order is reached, not the one holding BETTER~1.
     (with both present, bettercad-aaa's own short name is BETTER~2)

a sibling sorting before bettercad-deps whose basis is BETTE- not BETTER:
  exit=0  Qt DLLs deployed=4
  -> harmless. Membership is the six-character 8.3 basis, not similarity.

So the predicate is: among the dependency prefix's siblings that share its
six-character 8.3 basis, one sorts before it by case-insensitive name.
Equal '~N' short names are NOT required -- bettercad-aaa took the lookup
while holding a distinct number. Removing the sibling fixes it; recreating
it breaks it again.
